    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:4061032714",
   "kind": "interface",
   "other_replies": [],
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "This is a weird situation for the user: Trying to resend a transaction is refused with \"Ignoring unnecessary request to schedule an already scheduled transaction\"",
   "settled_by": null,
   "status": "open",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36277#discussion_r4061032714"
  },
  {
   "after_reply": "no_reply",
   "after_reply_note": "",
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-09-21",
   "author": "mzumsande",
   "author_replies": [],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "retry logic becomes effectively dead code because reaching 1000 resend attempts takes impractically long",
   "hash": "542db18ff6dffeb2",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-22T01:16:33+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260922-0113",
     "cause": "rc:4065921818",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:4065921818",
   "kind": "maintenance",
   "other_replies": [],
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "Now the retry is basically dead code, since it will take a long time until 1000 resend attempts are reached - I think it might as well be removed.",
   "settled_by": null,
   "status": "open",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36277#discussion_r4065921818"
  },
  {
   "after_reply": "unclear",
   "after_reply_note": "author noted the tradeoff avoiding extra disconnect tracking and asked for reviewer preference",
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-09-21",
   "author": "mzumsande",
   "author_replies": [
    "rc:4067384104"
   ],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "transactions are kept in memory indefinitely until node restart or maximum limit, increasing resource usage",
   "hash": "e3da1e0842ec1629",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-22T01:16:33+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260922-0113",
     "cause": "rc:4066000330",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:4066000330",
   "kind": "safety",
   "other_replies": [],
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "This would lead to a potential unexpected increase in resource usage - before, we'd only keep transactions while they were in flight, and the shared pointer would be released",
   "settled_by": null,
   "status": "open",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36277#discussion_r4066000330"
  },
  {
   "after_reply": "no_reply",
   "after_reply_note": "",
   "association": "MEMBER",
   "at": "2026-09-21",
   "author": "mzumsande",
   "author_replies": [],
   "blocking": false,
   "fix": null,
   "harm": "a peer disconnecting without answering pong could cause Remove() to steal connection retry slots from unrelated transactions",
   "hash": "fef57b9f8e2ac461",
   "history": [
    {
     "at": "2026-09-22T01:16:33+00:00",
     "blocking": false,
     "by": "run:20260922-0113",
     "cause": "rc:4066104589",
     "status": "open"
    }
   ],
   "id": "rc:4066104589",
   "kind": "correctness",
   "other_replies": [],
   "pin": null,
   "quote": "now a peer that completed the handshake (`fDisconnect=true`) but doesn't answer the pong would not get a `peer_ack`, but also wouldn't get a try back, so if we then call `Remove()` it could steal slots from other, unrelated transactions.",
   "settled_by": null,
   "status": "open",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36277#discussion_r4066104589"
  }
 ],
